!===============================================================================
! user_nl_cam_PIPD -- MMPPE PI (1850) / PD (2025) production-run history output
!===============================================================================
! Purpose: history-output configuration for the actual MMPPE PI and PD
! experiments (MMPPE-info/MMPPE.md, "PPE Experiments" table), as opposed to
! MMPPE-info/user_nl_cam, which is the CTL spin-up file scoped ONLY to the 14
! One-At-a-Time "Variables to test". This file targets the full "Model Output
! Variables" tables (6-hourly Instantaneous, 6-hourly Instantaneous (optional),
! Monthly Mean).
!
! PI and PD differ only in emissions/nudging-target-year/forcing inputs (see
! MMPPE.md's "PPE Experiments" table) -- NOT in what gets written to history.
! This same file is intended to be used verbatim for both the PI and PD cases
! (and for the 1-year CTL/PPE spin-ups feeding into them); only the forcing/
! emissions/compset configuration (not covered here -- out of scope per this
! file's purpose) should differ between the two. Nudging setup (ERA5 winds,
! ~6hr relaxation above ~2km) is also out of scope here; it lives in its own
! namelist block (nudging_nl) and was intentionally not addressed by this file.
!
! Field derivation: full match/derivation notes for every field below are in
! MMPPE-info/6hourly_variable_mapping.txt and
! MMPPE-info/monthly_mean_variable_mapping.txt -- read those first; this file
! only summarizes the CESM field name(s) chosen per MMPPE variable. MATCH
! quality codes (EXACT/CLOSE/APPROX/DERIVED/NONE-BEST) are as defined there.
!
! Scope decisions made when building this file (see conversation that
! produced it -- flagging here since they materially affect run cost/output):
!   1. COSP/MODIS optional table: INCLUDED, on its own history tape (h1),
!      since MMPPE.md calls COSP "highly desirable for models with COSP".
!      Requires the case to be configured with -cosp (and the MODIS
!      simulator sub-package on) at CARBON/build time -- this user_nl_cam
!      alone does not turn COSP on. If COSP is not actually enabled for a
!      given case, fincl2/nhtfrq(2)/mfilt(2) below will just produce empty/
!      missing output and should be commented out.
!   2. Aerosol-free TOA fluxes (rsut_na/rsutcs_na/rlut_na/rlutcs_na):
!      INCLUDED, via a diagnostic ("double-call") radiation calculation
!      configured through rad_diag_1 below (see that section's own notes --
!      it is adapted from the working example in
!      test/system/nl_files/rad_diag_mam, with all aerosol mode entries
!      dropped rather than substituted, since the analogous MMPPE fields ask
!      for a truly aerosol-free flux, not a partially-aerosol-free one).
!   3. Fields with no native CESM field and no reasonable post-processing
!      derivation ("NONE-BEST" with no formula given in the mapping files):
!      OMITTED from fincl (they cannot be requested -- there is no addfld
!      name for them) and instead listed in the "NOT AVAILABLE" comment
!      block at the end of this file, so nothing is silently dropped from
!      the MMPPE variable list without a record of why.
!   4. DERIVED fields that are sums across aerosol modes/species (e.g. SO4 =
!      so4_a1+so4_a2+so4_a3) or unit conversions (e.g. DMS mol/mol ->
!      kg/kg): the INDIVIDUAL per-mode/native-unit component fields are
!      included in fincl so the sum/conversion can be done in
!      post-processing; CAM history cannot do runtime arithmetic across
!      fields.
!
! NOT FINAL: MMPPE.md itself says "the output list and variable names are
! still being finalised" -- treat this file as a first production-ready pass
! against the CURRENT protocol text, not a frozen spec. Re-check against
! MMPPE.md and the two mapping .txt files before a real PI/PD submission run.
!===============================================================================

